    {
      "id": "5wrlbi4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Disease"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Diseases are broadly categorized into communicable, non-communicable, and deficiency diseases.",
        "Communicable diseases are caused by pathogens such as bacteria, viruses, fungi, and protozoa.",
        "Deficiency diseases arise from a prolonged lack of specific essential vitamins or minerals in the diet.",
        "The immune system provides defense via innate (present from birth) and acquired (developed) immunity.",
        "Vaccination activates the body's adaptive immunity to protect against specific pathogens."
      ],
      "id": "4e0fuxy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bedzbcg",
      "content": "• A disease is a condition that impairs normal body function."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ozszfg0",
      "content": "• It may cause pain, weakness, discomfort or dysfunction of organs."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "udahc60",
      "content": "• Diseases may be infectious or non‑infectious."
    },
    {
      "id": "0g4ygut",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Types of Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "crt4fd6",
      "content": "• Communicable diseases – Spread from one person to another."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8dmudul",
      "content": "• Non‑communicable diseases – Do not spread between individuals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "23uhcrk",
      "content": "• Deficiency diseases – Caused by lack of nutrients."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4x0wkx4",
      "content": "• Hereditary diseases – Passed through genes."
    },
    {
